---
import RosterEaseLayout from "../layouts/RosterEaseLayout.astro";

const quickFacts = [
  {
    label: "Applies to",
    value: "RosterEase website, iPhone app, and iPad app",
  },
  {
    label: "Optional permissions",
    value: "Calendar, camera, photos, location, microphone and others, each only when you choose",
  },
  {
    label: "Support",
    value: "Use the contact page",
    href: "/contact/",
  },
  {
    label: "Effective date",
    value: "7 August 2026",
  },
];

const sections = [
  {
    title: "Overview",
    paragraphs: [
      "This Privacy Policy explains how RosterEase handles information when you use the RosterEase website or mobile app.",
      "It is written as a plain policy for the current version of the product and should be read alongside Apple's TestFlight and App Store privacy information where those services are involved.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Information you provide",
    paragraphs: [
      "If you contact RosterEase, you may provide information such as your name, email address, and anything else you include in the message.",
      "If you use the app, you may choose to add or import schedule information, shift types, workplaces, clients, visit stops, addresses, notes, travel preferences, calendar choices, backup choices, and app settings.",
      "RosterEase does not require you to send roster content to support. If you choose to send examples, use redacted examples wherever possible.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Roster examples, imports, and redaction",
    paragraphs: [
      "Do not send sensitive roster, import, client, patient, employee, medical, support, payroll, or workplace-confidential information to RosterEase.",
      "Before sending screenshots, PDFs, pasted roster text, client lists, route examples, or failed-import examples, redact names, addresses, phone numbers, employee IDs, client identifiers, private notes, medical or support notes, and any other sensitive details.",
      "You are responsible for deciding what you are allowed to import into the app and what you are allowed to share with RosterEase for support. RosterEase cannot control what an end user chooses to import, paste, upload, screenshot, or send.",
      "RosterEase does not want or intentionally store sensitive roster/import examples. If sensitive information is submitted accidentally, RosterEase will use it only to understand the support request and will promptly delete it where feasible, unless retention is required for legal, security, or abuse-prevention reasons.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "App data and optional permissions",
    paragraphs: [
      "RosterEase is designed so roster, workplace, client, visit, and preference data can remain on your device. The app does not require a RosterEase account for this local planning data.",
      "Supported imports from files, images, PDFs, pasted text, and the clipboard are processed on-device. When OCR is needed for an image or scanned PDF, RosterEase uses on-device text recognition; results can be imperfect and should be reviewed before you apply them.",
      "If you choose to use optional permissions such as calendar, camera, photo, file, clipboard, location, microphone, or speech recognition access, that access is used only for the feature you asked the app to perform.",
      "Location is used only when you attach a location to a note or check-in, or, in Shifts with location review turned on, to notice arrivals and departures within 150 m of a workplace you have pinned, including while the app is closed if you allow Always access. Place names for note locations are looked up with Apple when shown.",
      "Voice notes and dictation are transcribed on your device. RosterEase does not send audio to a transcription server.",
      "For example, calendar access may be used to write shifts to a calendar you choose, and photo or file access may be used to import roster or client information into the app. Calendar events show the shift and workplace with generic RosterEase notes by default; each day's Shift info is added only if you turn on Include Shift Info. Private notes stay in the app.",
      "You can manage optional permissions through iOS or iPadOS Settings. Turning off a permission may limit the related feature but does not stop you from using the rest of the app.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Local performance reports",
    paragraphs: [
      "RosterEase can keep optional performance and crash summaries from Apple's MetricKit on your device. This is off unless you turn it on during setup or in Settings > About > Local performance reports. Declining changes no other feature.",
      "Kept, as numbers only: report intervals; CPU time, peak memory and disk writes; counts of crashes, hangs and resource exceptions; and the app and iOS version.",
      "Not kept: raw reports or stack traces, names, roster or client records, notes, locations, file paths, account IDs, keys, or device identifiers.",
      "Only reports covering time after you turned the option on are accepted. Reports stay on your device, are excluded from app backups, and are limited to 7 days, 20 reports and 10 MiB, with the oldest removed first. Expired reports are removed the next time the app runs, not while it is closed.",
      "Turning the option off stops collection and deletes the stored reports. If deletion fails, the app tells you and lets you retry. It cannot remove Apple's own device diagnostics or copies you have already shared.",
      "Nothing is sent automatically. To share reports, you authenticate with Face ID, Touch ID or your passcode, review the exact file, and choose where to send it through the share sheet. RosterEase cannot delete copies you have shared. Apple's own analytics and sharing settings are separate from this choice.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Backup and restore",
    paragraphs: [
      "A backup can include your roster, workplace, client, visit, note, and preference data. Backups are created when you save one in the app, or weekly to a folder you choose if you turn on Weekly Automatic Backup.",
      "Backups are encrypted with your backup key. RosterEase creates the key and keeps it in your device Keychain; it syncs with iCloud Keychain when that is on. You choose where backups are saved through Apple's file picker and other Apple system surfaces.",
      "RosterEase does not upload or retain exported backup files on its own backend. If you save or share the file through iCloud Drive, Files, a messaging app, or another destination/provider, that provider's handling, retention, and deletion rules apply.",
      "Anyone with a backup file and its key may be able to restore its contents. Store and share them carefully. Encryption reduces risk but does not guarantee absolute security.",
      "Restore is user-initiated: you select the file, enter its backup key when required, and confirm replacing the current RosterEase data on your device.",
      "If you use Apple device backup, iCloud, or another system backup or restore feature, Apple or your chosen backup provider handles that data under their own terms and settings.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Website and technical information",
    paragraphs: [
      "When you visit the website, standard technical information may be received, such as browser type, device information, IP address, and normal request or diagnostic data.",
      "The website uses system fonts and local static assets; it does not intentionally load third-party font files from Google Fonts or another font CDN.",
      "RosterEase does not use ads, third-party analytics, or tracking, and does not operate a custom backend that collects app data. Optional local performance reports stay on your device unless you choose to share them. The website host may still receive the normal technical request information described above.",
      "This information may be used to operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the website.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "How information is used",
    paragraphs: [
      "Information may be used to operate, maintain, and improve the website and app, provide the features you request, respond to support messages, and protect the security and integrity of the service.",
      "If you use optional product features, the related information is used only to provide those features. Apple Maps travel estimates are off by default; if enabled, RosterEase uses address text for estimates and does not include client names or notes in the estimate request.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Sharing",
    paragraphs: [
      "RosterEase does not sell personal information or use it for third-party advertising.",
      "Information may be processed by providers used to operate the website, email support, Apple platform distribution, TestFlight crash and feedback reporting, optional Apple Maps estimates and place-name lookups, and any destination you choose when sharing a diagnostics or performance report.",
      "These providers are used only as reasonably necessary to operate, secure, support, or improve RosterEase, comply with law, enforce terms, or protect rights, safety, and security.",
      "Apple may process information when you download, install, test, review, or submit feedback through TestFlight or the App Store. That Apple-controlled processing is covered by Apple's privacy terms.",
      "Some providers may process information outside Australia, including in countries where Apple, website hosting, and email providers operate.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Retention",
    paragraphs: [
      "Information is retained for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the website or app, fulfill legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce agreements.",
      "Information stored in the app may remain on your device until you delete it, remove the app, or replace it with new imported or restored data.",
      "Redacted support examples may be retained only as long as reasonably needed to respond or improve import handling. Accidental sensitive submissions will be deleted promptly where feasible.",
      "You can ask RosterEase to delete support correspondence or redacted examples you have sent, subject to legal, security, abuse-prevention, and backup-retention limits.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Security",
    paragraphs: [
      "Reasonable steps are taken to protect information, but no method of storage or transmission is completely secure.",
      "Absolute security cannot be guaranteed.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Access, correction, deletion, and complaints",
    paragraphs: [
      'You can ask RosterEase to access, correct, or delete personal information held by RosterEase by using the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.',
      "This mainly covers support messages, feedback, crash or diagnostic information available to the developer, and any examples you choose to send.",
      "RosterEase cannot directly delete information stored only on your device, including local performance reports. You can delete that in the app where available, turn off local performance reports to delete them, remove imported data, revoke permissions in iOS or iPadOS Settings, or uninstall the app.",
      "Privacy complaints can be sent through the contact page and will be reviewed and responded to within a reasonable time.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Your choices",
    paragraphs: [
      "You can choose whether to contact RosterEase and what information to include.",
      "You can choose whether to grant optional app permissions such as calendar, camera, photos, files, clipboard, location, microphone, or speech recognition access. You can also choose whether to enable Apple Maps estimates, whether Shift info is copied into Calendar events, and whether to keep local performance reports.",
      "You can delete app data from inside the app where available, by removing the app, or by changing the relevant iOS or iPadOS permission settings.",
      "You can stop using the app or website at any time.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "TestFlight beta participation",
    paragraphs: [
      "RosterEase is available on the App Store, with optional beta testing through Apple's TestFlight programme. If you join the beta, Apple may collect information such as your TestFlight account details, device and OS version, app installs, crash logs, and any feedback you submit through TestFlight.",
      'That information is handled by Apple under their TestFlight privacy terms: <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/test-flight/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/test-flight</a>.',
      "Apple may make crash logs, screenshots, feedback text, diagnostics, tester contact or account metadata, and related TestFlight information available to the developer.",
      "Crash and feedback data shared with the developer through TestFlight is used only to diagnose issues and improve current and upcoming versions of the app.",
      "Public support and privacy questions should use the contact page on this site.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Contact",
    paragraphs: [
      'If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> on this site.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<RosterEaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Read the RosterEase Privacy Policy for the website, TestFlight build, iPhone app, and iPad app."
>
  <section class="re-subpage-hero">
    <div class="re-shell re-subpage-hero__grid re-subpage-hero__grid--policy">
      <div class="re-subpage-hero__copy">
        <p class="re-kicker">Privacy Policy</p>
        <h1 class="re-page-title">A plain policy for the current version of RosterEase.</h1>
        <p class="re-lede re-subpage-hero__lede">
          This page covers the RosterEase website and mobile app, including optional import,
          calendar sync, visit route, notes, location review, widget, backup, performance report,
          and TestFlight feedback features.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="re-fact-sheet">
        <span class="re-fact-sheet__label">Quick facts</span>
        <dl class="re-fact-sheet__list">
          {
            quickFacts.map((fact) => (
              <div class="re-fact-sheet__row">
                <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
                <dd>
                  {fact.href ? <a href={fact.href}>{fact.value}</a> : fact.value}
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="re-policy-section">
    <div class="re-shell re-policy-grid">
      <nav class="re-policy-nav" aria-label="Policy contents">
        <span class="re-policy-nav__label">Contents</span>
        <ol>
          {
            sections.map((section, index) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`#policy-${index + 1}`}>{section.title}</a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="re-policy-stack">
        {
          sections.map((section, index) => (
            <article class="re-policy-article" id={`policy-${index + 1}`}>
              <span class="re-policy-article__number" aria-hidden="true">
                {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
              </span>

              <div class="re-policy-article__body">
                <h2>{section.title}</h2>
                {section.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p set:html={paragraph} />)}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</RosterEaseLayout>
